WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.590
- I see my patients repeating

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.560
these skincare mistakes all the time.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.000
And I've spoken to plenty of
my dermatologist colleagues

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.310
and we agree, this is the top list.

00:00:09.014 --> 00:00:11.164
Popping those good old pimples.

00:00:11.164 --> 00:00:14.104
As a general rule, you should
not pop your own pimples.

00:00:14.104 --> 00:00:15.754
If you do attempt to pop a pimple

00:00:15.754 --> 00:00:17.334
and ended up breaking your skin barrier,

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:19.404
you risk permanent acne scarring.

00:00:19.404 --> 00:00:21.184
If your pimple contains infected pus,

00:00:21.184 --> 00:00:24.444
popping can spread bacteria
into other pores, hair follicles

00:00:24.444 --> 00:00:26.144
and create even a worse outbreak.

00:00:26.144 --> 00:00:28.094
In fact, popping a
pimple can actually delay

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.264
your body's natural healing process.

00:00:30.264 --> 00:00:32.024
This is where spa
treatments come in handy.

00:00:32.024 --> 00:00:34.594
Pouring on hydrogen peroxide and alcohol.

00:00:34.594 --> 00:00:36.364
Despite what we've been told as kids,

00:00:36.364 --> 00:00:39.104
using hydrogen peroxide or rubbing alcohol

00:00:39.104 --> 00:00:41.333
to clean an injury can
actually harm the tissue

00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:42.794
and delay healing.

00:00:42.794 --> 00:00:44.284
The best way to clean a minor wound

00:00:44.284 --> 00:00:46.374
is with cool, running water and mild soap.

00:00:46.374 --> 00:00:48.134
Rinse the wound for at least five minutes

00:00:48.134 --> 00:00:50.064
to remove dirt, debris and bacteria.

00:00:50.064 --> 00:00:51.964
Wounds, however, that are large, deep

00:00:51.964 --> 00:00:54.824
or bleeding nonstop should
be treated by a professional,

00:00:54.824 --> 00:00:57.704
you know, one with scrubs like this.

00:00:57.704 --> 00:00:59.164
Shaving hard.

00:00:59.164 --> 00:01:01.094
When it comes to how hard
you should be pressing

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:02.504
the razorblade down on your skin,

00:01:02.504 --> 00:01:04.774
always remember, less is more.

00:01:04.774 --> 00:01:05.674
The harder you push down,

00:01:05.674 --> 00:01:07.644
the more uneven the skin surface becomes

00:01:07.644 --> 00:01:09.284
because the skin begins to dimple,

00:01:09.284 --> 00:01:11.074
and companies have tried to compensate

00:01:11.074 --> 00:01:12.284
for this common tendency,

00:01:12.284 --> 00:01:14.434
making razors that
resist shaving pressure,

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:17.254
but you will still get
a great nick-free shave

00:01:17.254 --> 00:01:18.884
if you use that light touch.

00:01:18.884 --> 00:01:21.394
Keeping wet clothes on for too long.

00:01:21.394 --> 00:01:23.354
I'm talking about the rain, the pool,

00:01:23.354 --> 00:01:24.634
the gym, whatever it is.

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:26.784
Wet and sweaty clothing can trap dust

00:01:26.784 --> 00:01:29.804
and dirt that clogs pores
and often leads to breakouts.

00:01:29.804 --> 00:01:31.574
Cotton is great at absorbing water,

00:01:31.574 --> 00:01:33.354
therefore deflecting body oil,

00:01:33.354 --> 00:01:35.024
but all this high-tech performance gear

00:01:35.024 --> 00:01:37.004
that we're wearing
actually deflects water,

00:01:37.004 --> 00:01:38.384
that's why it's moisture-wicking.

00:01:38.384 --> 00:01:41.034
However, it also absorbs body oils

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.964
and then the bacteria
feed on those body oils

00:01:42.964 --> 00:01:44.574
and release a really gross scent.

00:01:44.574 --> 00:01:47.314
On top of it, you put yourself
at higher risk for jock itch

00:01:47.314 --> 00:01:50.094
and other fungal infections,
which is no fun for your skin.

00:01:50.094 --> 00:01:51.834
Falling for social media fads.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:54.794
TikTok and social media
in general is loaded

00:01:54.794 --> 00:01:57.011
with skincare knowledge like this.

00:01:57.011 --> 00:01:59.214
(buzzer buzzing)
And this.

00:01:59.214 --> 00:02:00.577
And this.
- I look good

00:02:00.577 --> 00:02:02.228
with this kitty litter on my face.

00:02:02.228 --> 00:02:03.314
- But it's important to remember

00:02:03.314 --> 00:02:05.224
that miracle cures don't exist,

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:08.574
and some of the hacks we
see online are complete BS.

00:02:08.574 --> 00:02:10.454
Also, do not assume
what works for a friend

00:02:10.454 --> 00:02:11.604
or celeb will work for you.

00:02:11.604 --> 00:02:14.534
Everyone has unique skincare
needs, issues and goals.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.734
And it's probably important to add

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:16.884
that there's a lot of surgery

00:02:16.884 --> 00:02:18.219
and Photoshopping at play online.

00:02:18.219 --> 00:02:21.604
Taking long, hot showers.

00:02:21.604 --> 00:02:24.044
Hot showers are no bueno for your skin.

00:02:24.044 --> 00:02:25.794
They might be good for
your soul, but ideally,

00:02:25.794 --> 00:02:28.012
you should try and keep your
showers on the shorter side.

00:02:28.012 --> 00:02:30.944
And if you enjoy hot water,
you should keep it even shorter

00:02:30.944 --> 00:02:33.264
as that hot water can
strip the body of oils

00:02:33.264 --> 00:02:34.394
and dry out your skin.

00:02:34.394 --> 00:02:36.264
For my patients with eczema-prone skin,

00:02:36.264 --> 00:02:39.034
hot water actually draws
moisture away from the skin.

00:02:39.034 --> 00:02:40.724
And while it may feel good initially,

00:02:40.724 --> 00:02:43.444
frequent exposure can actually
exacerbate that eczema.

00:02:43.444 --> 00:02:45.414
Keeping small cuts and wounds covered.

00:02:45.414 --> 00:02:47.914
So many of my patients
believe the best way

00:02:47.914 --> 00:02:50.824
to let a minor wound heal
is by letting it dry out.

00:02:50.824 --> 00:02:51.829
Actually, keeping it covered

00:02:51.829 --> 00:02:54.234
and allowing it to stay
moist has been shown

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.624
to heal better with a
healthier layer of new skin,

00:02:58.187 --> 00:03:00.287
Forgetting that skin is its own organ.

00:03:00.287 --> 00:03:01.787
The skin needs to be looked after

00:03:01.787 --> 00:03:03.967
just like all the other
organs in our bodies.

00:03:03.967 --> 00:03:06.087
Consider getting regular skin exams

00:03:06.087 --> 00:03:09.377
especially if you have a family
history, use tanning beds,

00:03:09.377 --> 00:03:11.227
or had many sunburns in the past.

00:03:11.227 --> 00:03:12.357
Knowing what's normal for you

00:03:12.357 --> 00:03:13.887
is incredibly important as well.

00:03:13.887 --> 00:03:16.587
So if you see a mold
change or a new one appear,

00:03:16.587 --> 00:03:18.477
that's definitely worth
a visit to your doctor.

00:03:18.477 --> 00:03:20.627
No shade, no sunblock.

00:03:20.627 --> 00:03:23.107
You really need sunscreen every day.

00:03:23.107 --> 00:03:26.037
Yes, even when it's cloudy,
raining, or snowing.

00:03:26.037 --> 00:03:28.084
Ever go skiing and not wear sunblock?

00:03:28.084 --> 00:03:29.087
- [Crowd] Ouch!

00:03:29.087 --> 00:03:31.677
- Sun exposure causes
sunspots, skin damage,

00:03:31.677 --> 00:03:33.137
and even lead to skin cancer.

00:03:33.137 --> 00:03:36.677
Using a simple daily
moisturizer/sunscreen combo is best

00:03:36.677 --> 00:03:38.234
but make sure it's at least 30 SPF.

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:40.887
And don't forget to apply
it to the ears and lips

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.847
as they're the most commonly missed areas.

00:03:42.847 --> 00:03:44.587
Skipping the good old neck.

00:03:44.587 --> 00:03:47.027
If your skincare routine
stops at your jawline,

00:03:47.027 --> 00:03:48.477
you're doing it wrong.

00:03:48.477 --> 00:03:49.737
Your neck needs some love too.

00:03:49.737 --> 00:03:52.137
In fact, the neck is one of
the first areas of the body

00:03:52.137 --> 00:03:53.337
to show signs of aging

00:03:53.337 --> 00:03:55.267
because the skin is
thinner than on your face.

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:56.827
Also staring at our cell phones

00:03:56.827 --> 00:03:59.757
with our necks bent all the
time isn't doing us any favors.

00:03:59.757 --> 00:04:02.397
Ever-changing routines
and too many products.

00:04:02.397 --> 00:04:04.787
As fun as it can be to
try new skincare products,

00:04:04.787 --> 00:04:06.687
doing so too frequently can create

00:04:06.687 --> 00:04:08.557
more questions and problems.

00:04:08.557 --> 00:04:11.007
Most ingredients will take
at least four to six weeks

00:04:11.007 --> 00:04:13.497
of consistent use before
noticeable changes.

00:04:13.497 --> 00:04:15.517
Also, know that if you
have a negative reaction,

00:04:15.517 --> 00:04:17.397
it's gonna be really hard
to pinpoint the cause

00:04:17.397 --> 00:04:20.007
if you introduce two to three
products simultaneously.

00:04:20.007 --> 00:04:22.027
Over-exfoliate with harsh scrubs.

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:24.397
While exfoliation is
important in moderation,

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:27.287
it's easy to overdo it
with exfoliating scrubs,

00:04:27.287 --> 00:04:29.307
especially when your skin is feeling dry.

00:04:29.307 --> 00:04:31.917
Overdoing it can cause
tiny tears in the skin,

00:04:31.917 --> 00:04:34.557
leading to the development
of a rash-like texture

00:04:34.557 --> 00:04:37.397
and uneven tone, like
patchy, red blotches.

00:04:37.397 --> 00:04:39.017
Breakouts are another common reaction,

00:04:39.017 --> 00:04:41.367
especially small, rough, bumpy pimples.

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:42.797
If you're using a scrub on your face,

00:04:42.797 --> 00:04:44.947
you should do it max two times per week.

00:04:44.947 --> 00:04:46.787
And when you're doing
it, please be gentle.

00:04:46.787 --> 00:04:48.177
Don't scrub your skin raw.

00:04:48.177 --> 00:04:49.397
Picking their skin.

00:04:49.397 --> 00:04:51.277
You may not even realize that you do it,

00:04:51.277 --> 00:04:54.317
but constantly picking at the
skin can cause irritation,

00:04:54.317 --> 00:04:56.627
inflamed skin and spread bacteria.

00:04:56.627 --> 00:04:59.287
The digits or our fingers
are the dirtiest parts

00:04:59.287 --> 00:05:01.737
of our bodies and harbor
all sorts of bacteria

00:05:01.737 --> 00:05:03.637
that should stay on the
outside of our skin.

00:05:03.637 --> 00:05:05.897
If this is a nervous
habit, try to break it

00:05:05.897 --> 00:05:07.887
by keeping your hands
busy with something else

00:05:07.887 --> 00:05:09.328
or perhaps asking for others

00:05:09.328 --> 00:05:11.187
to help point out when you're doing it

00:05:11.187 --> 00:05:12.147
without even knowing it.

00:05:12.147 --> 00:05:14.047
Fearing thy moisturizer.

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:16.547
Skin is meant to keep bad
things out of your body,

00:05:16.547 --> 00:05:19.687
and moisturizing is imperative
for a healthy skin barrier,

00:05:19.687 --> 00:05:21.107
which is why you shouldn't skip out

00:05:21.107 --> 00:05:22.587
on using moisturizers daily.

00:05:22.587 --> 00:05:24.027
Many of my patients with oily

00:05:24.027 --> 00:05:26.777
or acne-prone skin think they
should use this product less,

00:05:26.777 --> 00:05:27.737
but the reality is,

